    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 187,
        "text": "Thanks for coming, everyone. This is the weekly research meeting for the campus learning project. We need to decide whether to keep using the participation rate as our main measure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "4ffa2ba885260effdce9ef75f3a23d6fb442598e163f8759db47bc1bc450c7cc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 194,
        "sourceEnd": 376,
        "text": "Right. The participation rate is the percentage of students who attend at least one session each week. Last term it was 72 percent. This term it is 81 percent. The number looks good.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "ad9d97fbbb68bf640ad0a8bc400027ca469a763fa918f72f8bdfc5a93687851c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 384,
        "sourceEnd": 472,
        "text": "But does it really show learning? I mean, a student can attend and still not learn much.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "64538b652a4692617bebbb7ad1bd2c37956b3a91045bb34fa325adec7ed7dc00",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 479,
        "sourceEnd": 543,
        "text": "That's true. But it is easy to collect. We just count who comes.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "865f5e0d5ef5bf19393f9a8ac7faaf944095868661c4296ca4fe2b12fde97d34",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 551,
        "sourceEnd": 698,
        "text": "Sorry to interrupt, but I think we are missing something. Attendance is not the same as engagement. A student might sit in the room and do nothing.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "64e41b3579f21d5f7875d78904b8ddd0b4e8c56e25a0918c5be0cc53ef625242",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 706,
        "sourceEnd": 777,
        "text": "Exactly. So if we want to measure learning, we need a different metric.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ac00eb1288f573d1cb1e1c7634a7668f10a6535c0844b866ff060b6caf04880c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 784,
        "sourceEnd": 895,
        "text": "Wait, I didn't say the participation rate is useless. I said it is easy to collect. Those are different things.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "edeeca9b3ee157ea8efa7159033b691fe93eae68798a4a6c10b565795e1524e5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 903,
        "sourceEnd": 1016,
        "text": "You're right. Sorry. Let me rephrase. The participation rate is easy to collect, but it may not measure learning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "59927af22a5180e95c45b60cabe950a898c4bc8e600f20ea8d6c3a4a409e1237",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1024,
        "sourceEnd": 1091,
        "text": "Good. So what else can we use? We have the end-of-term test scores.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "3f536498511c8bca40d35908442bbeb1cd10cac3fa6e2d45a030744e1671f843",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1098,
        "sourceEnd": 1168,
        "text": "Yes, but those come only once a term. They don't show weekly progress.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "770dcc992e6f8be5f4a2225dce6590a9cf85e2a7fae016be8e77183ec169e2dc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 1176,
        "sourceEnd": 1281,
        "text": "What about the short quizzes we give every two weeks? They are quick, and they show what students can do.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a59c59a1a3bdb4edd6797d3db74b8c3be6f504d861d66854099b558477c6d2d6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1289,
        "sourceEnd": 1419,
        "text": "That's a good idea. But if we use quiz scores, we need to make sure the quizzes are fair. Otherwise the metric will be unfair too.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "ca0a2498cff61c67cc0161312066872508aae046238df9d2c0fd0d2b43f429d3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1426,
        "sourceEnd": 1512,
        "text": "And if we change the metric, we have to explain it to the teachers. They will ask why.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "33f573534fc5255c291926a64ac6f90182047635a38efe495b2447c302d9b358",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 1520,
        "sourceEnd": 1673,
        "text": "We can explain that participation is an input measure, while quiz scores are an outcome measure. Inputs are what we do; outcomes are what students learn.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f1e3f20de16f56c2786afbfb6f172ebabfacd81d51acf448d37296a3baab87f1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1681,
        "sourceEnd": 1809,
        "text": "I like that distinction. So the participation rate tells us how many students come, but it does not tell us how much they learn.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "b6a167e6845763dbbb040175d7233707db20be91fd856aa84698e8d67a81adc7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1816,
        "sourceEnd": 1899,
        "text": "OK, but I still think attendance matters. If students don't come, they can't learn.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "118a6367c65516b52ae0671e1f7f71d819fd6387ff5e5166bdb6b5b8a8d5445a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 1907,
        "sourceEnd": 2012,
        "text": "True. So maybe we should keep both. Use participation to check access, and use quizzes to check learning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "ba6ffb6e84ed101711abe16f9ba056568f3aa4b7aa2055b9b38f84c45f7af04a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2020,
        "sourceEnd": 2157,
        "text": "That sounds balanced. But we need to be careful. If we report both, people may focus only on the participation rate because it is higher.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "6d35a4113633bf2cbd1a89f90b7c955ef0e57ac031e8048e26044ff2957944b7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2164,
        "sourceEnd": 2305,
        "text": "That's a real risk. The participation rate is 81 percent, but the average quiz score is only 64 percent. If we report both, the gap is clear.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8a0ec9aa08f50aee0f64a1befe74f6a37398a43b4124d53b81dacf5e38dc6732",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 2313,
        "sourceEnd": 2399,
        "text": "And if we report only participation, the gap is hidden. That's why the metric matters.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "a795906cff0b67db1fa35a2d5956cf68f1cdba886e39cde875fe9096024fca3c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2407,
        "sourceEnd": 2555,
        "text": "So our recommendation is to report both, but to explain that they measure different things. Participation measures access; quizzes measure learning.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d5293450b6bd00cee6cc3e37a59bf21e5330c92f3a97dc886f404eb115763ca3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2562,
        "sourceEnd": 2714,
        "text": "I agree. But we should also check whether the quizzes are reliable. If the quizzes are too easy, the scores will be high and the metric will mislead us.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "8ce95e9fec114aef067de5824b7fc06fd6cc70e91ec3bff887e74424b511c427",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 2722,
        "sourceEnd": 2799,
        "text": "Good point. We can ask two teachers to review the quizzes before we use them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "abe7e86647cb2771c7079980ff2f8b97c8663323f07f2614b159d583073c6709",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2807,
        "sourceEnd": 2968,
        "text": "OK. So the plan is: keep the participation rate as an access measure, add quiz scores as a learning measure, and review the quizzes for fairness. Any objections?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "16b96ed78e11cc1e42eeea62853f08b1e61ef90b0eb2ddc0247acd1b3f850046",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2975,
        "sourceEnd": 2988,
        "text": "None from me.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "81f51a2451ed98f9f17aa392e30f8d920a10b00ca16800a39a958e17eb52c97c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "lena",
        "speaker": "Lena",
        "sourceStart": 2996,
        "sourceEnd": 3085,
        "text": "None. But can we also look at the dropout rate? If students leave, that is important too.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "0850622c65fe5edc7009c8088056f504a8782296a3aefd8f6751a479ababc3aa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3093,
        "sourceEnd": 3199,
        "text": "Yes, good idea. We can add the dropout rate as a third measure. But let's not make the report too complex.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "0da9797a5da512f8152b9208ae4177e47e09386fb0850d2594a747b20ec759db",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 3206,
        "sourceEnd": 3314,
        "text": "Agreed. So three measures: participation, quiz scores, and dropout rate. And we explain what each one means.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-EricNeural",
        "textHash": "f72ea5197c814a07294744160bcb7c26443fffe15d423eaddc8602a38d543edd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 3322,
        "sourceEnd": 3404,
        "text": "Perfect. I'll write the draft and send it to you both by Friday. Thanks, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "614c6c019db277b0b6d544f4063bde404bff8bc981ebe72015f4130ecb5f2c27",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
